  {
   "label": "atom",
   "method": false,
   "detail": "atom(name, { type, params?, body | from, doc? })",
   "info": "Declare an atom: one typed, parameterised definition for a magic string (docs/ATOMS.md). Types: mini, sound, bank, note, chord, scale, voicing, progression, gate, point, tapref, slot, hook, name, text. Header statement; it is removed when the program is compiled. Compile pass built (#61); editor, intellisense, hooks / model / pads / maps and pack wiring built (#63). Graph cards and the reference popover are coming (#64).",
   "category": "atoms"
  },
  {
   "label": "atoms",
   "method": false,
   "detail": "atoms.<name> / atoms.<name>({ param: value })",
   "info": "Reference an atom anywhere its string would go. Pattern types compile to a double-quoted string, name types to a single-quoted one. Ops: .seq() .stack() .alt() .rep() .slow() .euclid() (mini), .union() .shift() (gate), .after() .before() .to() (point), .facet() .in() (tapref/name), .pipe() .wrap() (hook). Catalog namespaces need no declaration: atoms.snd.<sound>, atoms.bank.<bank>, atoms.scale.<mode>({ root }), atoms.chord.<quality>({ root }); an unknown sound warns W_ATOM_UNKNOWN_SOUND. Compile pass built (#61), extract / parse / inline built (#62), consumers built (#63): shape-filtered completion, atoms. member completion, signature help, the \"use atoms.name\" action on a matching string literal, scrub / chips / steps editors on reference args, and $atom in hooks, model, pads, boards and maps. Graph cards and the reference popover are coming (#64).",
   "category": "atoms"
  },
  {
   "label": "voxBank",
   "method": false,
   "detail": "voxBank(name | url)",
